  "slug": "transcription-factor-e601",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications pair new genome, ancestry, simulation, and population-statistic methods with explicit validation against known standards.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational inference from incomplete or indirect genomic data, with methods judged against explicit standards. ImpuT2T uses a panel of T2T pangenome assemblies to patch gaps in inexpensive HiFi human genome assemblies and reports outperforming existing patching approaches. Gnomix provides local ancestry inference with Gnofix phase correction, reporting higher accuracy and speed along with shareable portable models. simPIC simulates single-cell ATAC-seq paired-insertion counts across individuals and populations with known ground truth. The pixy update adds missing-data-unbiased Watterson's theta and Tajima's D alongside arbitrary ploidy and multiallelic support. The 320 phased East Asian assemblies expose novel sequences, gene gains, and structural variants and inversions. What is new is the breadth of targets, spanning haplotype-resolved assemblies to population summary statistics, each tied to ground truth or comparative evaluation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-31"
}
